      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T0OROUT",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: carry-out of stage 0, Y = NAND(NOT(C1), NOT(C2)) = C1 OR C2 = majority(A0, B0, C0) \u2014 copy 1 of 10: the ripple carry C1 fans out onto stage 1\u0027s 10 carry-in pins, one waveguide per pin, so the whole carry-OR subtree is duplicated per consumer; this copy feeds T1H2N1A.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage\u0027s carry-out, which must reach the next stage\u0027s several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_8e585fb88e5d4151b97e22daff110566",
        "IdGuid": "62654b0c-0901-4714-8bf3-1ba1387d2133",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
